     "description": "The census tract represents small-area neighborhood units, while the census block is the smallest geographic unit used by the United States Census Bureau for tabulating data. Census tracts and blocks allow for the analysis of demographic and housing information. The field contains the Census Tract ID and Census Block ID as one string with both IDs separated by a period. This string is derived from the 2020 Census.",
